# Documentation

- All project documentation lives in the `docs/` folder (and its subfolders).
- Do not create documentation outside `docs/` unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Every document filename must be prefixed with the date in ISO format: `YYYY-MM-DD`.
  - Correct: `docs/2026-08-12-auth-overview.md`
  - Incorrect: `docs/auth-overview.md`
- Prefer clear, kebab-case titles after the date prefix.
- When updating an existing dated document, edit that file in place. Create a new dated file only when starting a distinct document or a new revision the user asked to keep separately.
- Organize by purpose when helpful, still under `docs/`:
  - `docs/prd/` — product requirement documents
  - `docs/plans/` — implementation plans
  - `docs/design/` — design system and UI guidance
